// The collection: the themes in production (owner, 2026-11-10: "they will go into production"). These are the themes the owner liked
// consistently from round 27 to round 38, each exactly as judged in round 38 (v1: vibrance follows intensity), and the light
// themes chosen in rounds 40–42. Each entry is
// the frozen specification of one judged theme, copied from the judging registry (generated/concept-lab/rate/themes.jsonl),
// and the id that hashes it, so a production theme cannot drift from what was judged: tests/video_renderer.test.ts recomputes
// every id. To add a theme, copy its registry entry; a changed theme is a new theme, judged again under a new name.
// Pure data: palettes.js gives each theme its scheme (named by its id, as the judging stills are drawn); look.js its look.
// Round 45 (owner, 13 November): variations the owner likes as much as their theme follow it directly (golden moon, moonlit bars,
// the three Rothkos, the two Cyanotypes, deeper dusk, gold leaf, Red Lacquer, deeper forest, ivory and red-sun Paper, Black Iris
// with a moon). They are themes like any other; how often near-identical ones are drawn is to be decided with the sampling. Three
// themes were replaced by the variation preferred to them: Lily White (fresh green), Cobalt and Chartreuse (white moon), Black Iris
// (thin strands).
// Round 46 (owner, 13 November), the same way: Cobalt with a lime bar; Forest Green with a cream moon and on a pine night; Amber and
// Violet, Sumi and Amber, Pine and Amber (the amber theme with other bars); Cerulean and Coral on a night ground, with the title or
// a cream moon. Stone is new.
// Rounds 47 and 48 (owner, 13 November). Replaced by the version preferred: Hokusai (black line), Silver and Rust (lighter ivory),
// Peony (dusty rose bars on warm white), Cut-outs (half cream), Cerulean and Coral (deeper ground). Added beside their theme: Hokusai
// bluer with the black line, Amber and Indigo, Cerulean and Coral deeper with a cream moon, Stone cool and Stone pencil → ink. New:
// Linen, Sage, Sky; the rooms after Rothko, Sea Moon and Olive Moon after Jungle Moon, Copper, Bronze, Lantern, Campfire, Ash and
// Ember, Slate Grey.
// Round 49 (owner, 14 November). Added: Brown Room with a cream hot bar, Dusk, Moss and Steel Room; Paper on Stone's and Sky's
// grounds; Dune and cool Stone with pencil → ink; Lantern with a cream bar; Gold and Cream on two grounds; Winter Moon (two bars)
// and Starry Night, which carry a crescent.
